{
  "case_id": "2006-06-134",
  "document_hash": "dab354da5bab5bf176bb9a36622a4a1a803fd15d9cf8ee3e8f9f5bd9c328e2b7",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-06-134",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dab354da5bab5bf176bb9a36622a4a1a803fd15d9cf8ee3e8f9f5bd9c328e2b7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dab354da5bab-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument first this morning in case 06-134, The Permanent Mission of India to the United Nations et al. vs. The City of New York."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "John J.P. Howley",
      "case_id": "2006-06-134",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dab354da5bab5bf176bb9a36622a4a1a803fd15d9cf8ee3e8f9f5bd9c328e2b7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dab354da5bab-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "These are tax enforcement lawsuits. If jurisdiction existed, the only issue a court would decide is whether a tax is owed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-06-134",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dab354da5bab5bf176bb9a36622a4a1a803fd15d9cf8ee3e8f9f5bd9c328e2b7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dab354da5bab-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: But it would clearly come within the property right exception, wouldn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-06-134",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dab354da5bab5bf176bb9a36622a4a1a803fd15d9cf8ee3e8f9f5bd9c328e2b7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dab354da5bab-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But what New York is seeking is an interest in land and a lien is an interest in the land. It runs with the land, doesn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "John J.P. Howley",
      "case_id": "2006-06-134",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dab354da5bab5bf176bb9a36622a4a1a803fd15d9cf8ee3e8f9f5bd9c328e2b7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dab354da5bab-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HOWLEY: I do not dispute that a lien holder has an interest, a security interest in the property. But Congress did not write in Section 1605(a)(4) all interests that are in issue in property."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-06-134",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dab354da5bab5bf176bb9a36622a4a1a803fd15d9cf8ee3e8f9f5bd9c328e2b7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dab354da5bab-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: What was your distinction between a mortgage and a tax lien?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-06-134",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dab354da5bab5bf176bb9a36622a4a1a803fd15d9cf8ee3e8f9f5bd9c328e2b7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dab354da5bab-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Well, that brings up the basic question I have, is this a question of State law or Federal law?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-06-134",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dab354da5bab5bf176bb9a36622a4a1a803fd15d9cf8ee3e8f9f5bd9c328e2b7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dab354da5bab-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, under your theory, that lien would not be enforceable, is that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2006-06-134",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dab354da5bab5bf176bb9a36622a4a1a803fd15d9cf8ee3e8f9f5bd9c328e2b7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dab354da5bab-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, I don't think it's a right in property, Justice Scalia. The lien is a species of property, of intangible personal property, in the same sense that a cause of action would be, because after all what a lien is is essentially at bottom a claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-06-134",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dab354da5bab5bf176bb9a36622a4a1a803fd15d9cf8ee3e8f9f5bd9c328e2b7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dab354da5bab-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What about an easement? That doesn't involve any of those things. You can't exclude people and so forth."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2006-06-134",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dab354da5bab5bf176bb9a36622a4a1a803fd15d9cf8ee3e8f9f5bd9c328e2b7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dab354da5bab-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But it doesn't mean that the fact that we can't foreclose doesn't mean that we don't have a right in property."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-06-134",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dab354da5bab5bf176bb9a36622a4a1a803fd15d9cf8ee3e8f9f5bd9c328e2b7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dab354da5bab-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: May, may I just ask, for a kind of a footnote kind of question? I mean you referred again to the text. And if we are going to go on a very strict reading of the text as I understand it, you don't have to claim a right in property, you have to have a claim in -- in which someone's rights in immovable property are in issue."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Cardozo",
      "case_id": "2006-06-134",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dab354da5bab5bf176bb9a36622a4a1a803fd15d9cf8ee3e8f9f5bd9c328e2b7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dab354da5bab-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CARDOZO: I, I agree with that. And here today the right that India and Mongolia claim in their property is in issue, because we say you do not have the full right to your property and if this lien runs long enough, it's going to wipe out the value of their property completely."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-06-134",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dab354da5bab5bf176bb9a36622a4a1a803fd15d9cf8ee3e8f9f5bd9c328e2b7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dab354da5bab-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Now -- now I take it you under New York law and the law of most jurisdictions, the tax lien becomes a lien against the property before any judicial proceedings."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2006-06-134",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "dab354da5bab5bf176bb9a36622a4a1a803fd15d9cf8ee3e8f9f5bd9c328e2b7",
